INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'final_report' with arguments: {"investigation_summary": "Target: 2023 3CX DesktopApp software supply-chain compromise. Evidence chain from benchmark sources: Mandiant/Google Cloud SRC-003 states initial compromise vector was malicious software downloaded from Trading Technologies' website, specifically a tampered X_TRADER installer from an earlier software supply-chain compromise. On a 3CX employee machine, X_TRADER enabled the attackers to move laterally through 3CX, harvest credentials, and compromise both Windows and macOS build environments. On Windows, TAXHAUL and COLDCAT were deployed; COLDCAT persisted via IKEEXT DLL search-order hijacking with LocalSystem privileges. On macOS, POOLRAT persisted via Launch Daemons; earlier reporting called it SIMPLESEA, but Mandiant identified it as POOLRAT. The attackers then trojanized 3CX DesktopApp builds. Affected 3CX DesktopApp 18.12.416 and earlier ran SUDDENICON, which retrieved C2 URLs from encrypted icon files hosted on GitHub and downloaded ICONICSTEALER, a browser-information dataminer. Mandiant tracks the activity as UNC4736, a suspected North Korean nexus cluster, and assesses with moderate confidence that UNC4736 is related to financially motivated North Korean AppleJeus activity. It notes weak infrastructure overlap with suspected APT43 clusters UNC3782 and UNC4469. Mandiant's technical similarities between X_TRADER and 3CX include the same RC4 key, SIGFLIP, DAVESHELL, hardcoded cookie variable, and AES-256-GCM encryption. SRC-008 independently describes the chain as two linked supply-chain attacks: X_TRADER infected a 3CX employee, access spread to the 3CX development server, the installer was corrupted, and customers received the infected software. SRC-004 reports the trojanized MSI/macOS package, DLL and shellcode chain, C2 URLs from GitHub icons, infostealer, and Gopuram backdoor; it attributes the campaign to Lazarus with medium-to-high confidence based on Gopuram coexisting with AppleJeus, cryptocurrency targeting, shared loader shellcode/infrastructure, and domains previously attributed to Lazarus. SRC-002 reports North Korean attribution by CrowdStrike/SentinelOne, calls the operation Smooth Operator, says Gopuram was a final payload seen on fewer than 10 machines and targeted cryptocurrency firms, but also records uncertainty about the campaign's full goals. SRC-009 (Singapore CSA, 31 Mar 2023) confirms discovery of trojanized 3CX DesktopApp and lists affected Windows 18.12.407/416 and Mac 18.11.1213, 18.12.402/407/416; it says the app could harvest system information and steal data/stored credentials from Chrome, Edge, Brave, and Firefox profiles. SRC-007 identifies Lazarus Group as a North Korean state-sponsored group and warns public reporting uses Lazarus as an umbrella term and specific operations may be difficult to attribute with high confidence. Required report should distinguish Mandiant's cluster label UNC4736 from Kaspersky's Lazarus attribution and clearly label assessments/uncertainty. Cite only SRC-001 through SRC-009 as returned source IDs."}
